  {
   "n": 6,
   "type": "MSQ",
   "section": "Technical",
   "tags": "Technical • Data Science & Artificial Intelligence • +2 / -0.66",
   "html": "<p>Which of the following statement/statements is/are true?</p>",
   "options": [
    {
     "key": "A",
     "html": "Ternary search is more efficient than binary search for searching an element in the array."
    },
    {
     "key": "B",
     "html": "Strassen’s matrix multiplication method is a dynamic programming technique."
    },
    {
     "key": "C",
     "html": "Randomized quick sort is not an improvement over quick sort (traditional) for an already sorted array."
    },
    {
     "key": "D",
     "html": "Inorder traversal of a binary search tree is always in ascending order."
    }
   ],
   "answer": [
    "A",
    "B",
    "C",
    "D"
   ],
   "natRange": null,
   "answerText": "D, A, B, C",
   "marks": {
    "pos": 2,
    "neg": 0.66
   },
   "solution": "<p>(d)<br />\n(a) False: Ternary search takes more time when compared to binary search.<br />\n(b) False: Strassen&rsquo;s matrix multiplication is a divide and conquer technique.<br />\n(c) False: Randomized quick sort handles a sorted array better than traditional quick sort.</p>"
  },
